#!/bin/bash
# dsm-zsa14.sh (12.11.2026, queue-ar/dsmain/zsa14, a builder for ds-main-port) -- NOT a queue item; the body of
# 57-p4zyzzzzz-ds-r92zzzzzz-ref12zzzzzz-zsa14.sh. Log tag "RESULT xsa14 ", out runs/xdsm/zsa14 (SA14_OUT). A COPY of
# ref14/dsm-zsa14.sh (md5 74981d12, as staged 12.11.; tag xsa14 -> xsa14, knobs SA14_ -> SA14_; generated by zsa14/mkbody.py, every
# edit an asserted replacement; ref14's body not changed; unused functions kept): the SAME start words, guards, image checks (int9 ..
# int14c literals, int12's plugin md5), n-gram reuse (tools/ngramshare/ngshare.sh, TESTING.md BODY RULE), THE int14 PIN posted by fn4
# right after the start and READ BACK on fn4 and every rank (rankrb), A4's table + A11's ranged entries (copies of ref14's = yzint14c's,
# md5-checked, NOT re-benched), the same c8 / c16 harness (harness/ncmb3.py, the fixed prompt set reset per block), the staggered check
# (stack4/loadid.py run), ref14/ncmatch.py (copied: the matched-prompt newcomer sums) + zsa14/sa14sum.py + zsa14/steps.py (the
# coordinator's raw step lister, md5 569fd59b, copied).
# ONE ZERO-BUILD SCREEN: lever SA (ds41-sahb, fn4 stage_short N / stage_pick K; already in int14: "lever SA / HB (ds41-sahb) set up, off:
#   stage_short can arm the prefill stager for a step of 1025 .. 2112 tokens at the span's shared level") RE-READ on THE NEW DS BASE int14
#   with the fixed method (TESTING.md 12.11. "WINDOW QUANTUM"). SA arms the prefill stager for a step with prefill rows and >= N tokens at
#   the span's shared arena level (1025 .. 2112 rows: every c8 newcomer step, ~1.1k rows with 7 decode rows riding): the step's routed
#   pooled units are copied into a ring (RADIANCE_STAGE_SPAN=0's lent place, recalled for the step: ~1 GiB of arena loan a rank) and the
#   GEMMs read them there; stage_pick K copies only the units one of the last K stager-size steps routed (0 = every pooled unit, a loss
#   pre-move). Placement only (stager.h: the same bytes, the same kernel). RADIANCE_STAGE_MIXED stays unset (= 1: mixed passes may arm).
#   PRE-MOVE (12.11. usahb, LEVERS.md "SA / HB"): alone ~1.1k newcomers B 613.4 / 577.7 ms, pick 0 798.7, pick 1 588.0, pick 2 570.8 (step
#   level inconclusive); mb c8 SA -0.8 % on the old agg (window-quantum artefact); dropped, never re-read after the 12.11. riser move
#   (4-card H2D 61.5 -> 106.2 GB/s: the newcomer step is no longer link-bound, ~155 ms of DMA in a ~533 ms step; ~55-80 ms of host-tier
#   expert reads unhidden, inferred). Estimate: newcomer -30 .. -80 ms, c8 +1.1 .. +3.0 %, could be 0. RISK: each armed step recalls the
#   arena loan, so the decode steps right after may refill-miss -> read separately.
# IMAGE radiance-local:ds41-int14c-678c176f-579d0bc2-l (a7ca6bcdf07b), THE int14 PIN (= ref14's O = yzint14c's Z) + RADIANCE_FN4_AR_XPUSH_MIN
#   =1048576, MAXSEQS 16. ARMS, in-process on ONE fresh start (ngshare, no ATTACH, compose guard in the item):
#     B  = the int14 pin, SA off (stage_short 0, stage_pick 0: the base pin's)
#     S1 = B + stage_short SA14_SSN 1025 + stage_pick SA14_PICK1 1
#     S2 = B + stage_short SA14_SSN 1025 + stage_pick SA14_PICK2 2 (the pre-move screen's fastest pick)
# READINGS, in order:
#   1 IDENTITY FIRST (strict, T 0 greedy): the warm-up answers vs stock; a1 (greedy set c1 alone) under B / S1 / S2, each vs ref12's a1
#     (+ a1-B vs yzint14c's a1-Z); gs16 (all 16 in flight, cap 48) under SA14_GSARM S2 vs a1-S2; STRICT staggered ld under SA14_LDARM S2
#     vs a1-S2 (stack4/loadid.py run: fresh SA14_LDPF 8192-token prefills joining the probes' decode = mixed ~2.1k-row chunk steps at the
#     span level, where SA arms). ANY difference -> VIRHE and the item STOPS before every speed block. Engagement logged for every
#     identity read (GET /admin/fn4 "sahb": armed steps, staged GB); ld-S2 with 0 armed steps is a VIRHE (armed-step exactness not shown).
#   2 c8 WORK-BASED (harness --window gens --gens SA14_C8GN 2: exactly gens x 8 newcomer steps inside, both edges in decode-only time; the
#     same fixed prompts in every block), in-process SA14_GORDER "B S1 S2 S2 S1 B".
#   3 c16: one gens block (--gens SA14_C16GN 1 = 16 newcomer steps) for B and for the better SA arm by 2's agg (default S2).
# SUMMARY (zsa14/sa14sum.py, lines "SA14 ..."): per block and arm -- agg tok/s (tokens / window time); newcomer = the MATCHED-PROMPT sums
#   (ref14/ncmatch.py over the c8 gens blocks: the same fixed prompts' newcomer-step walls, next step line - its own, unclipped; c16 by
#   sa14sum's own tie, since a step line prints only its first 8 plan entries); decode-step p50 over ALL decode steps of the window AND over
#   the SA14_POST 10 decode steps right after each newcomer step (the refill-miss risk) and the rest; /stats at the window marks: staged /
#   stream / h2d GB, arena slot misses / drop_recall / fills; GET "sahb" over the block: armed steps, staged GB an armed step, pick kept /
#   dropped, loan recalled; engagement guard (S arms armed > 0, B 0); a steady-state cycle model per arm (B's decode steps a newcomer x the
#   arm's decode ms + its matched newcomer ms -> tok/s) next to the measured agg; a HEADLINE with the same-arm spread. steps.py's raw
#   listing per gens block -> c8/<block>-steps.txt (+ its in-window newcomer wall sum, INFO).
# ~24 min (start ~5.5 with the n-gram fill, identity ~5, c8 6 blocks ~8, c16 2 blocks ~3, summary ~1.5); BUDGET SA14_BUDGET_MIN 28 for the
#   sections (a section past it skipped, logged: c16 goes first), <= 30 with the summary. NO evict, no cc_sim, no power / host / fan
#   settings; production compose files read only; nothing profiled. At the end the raw snapshots go into one tar.gz, the engine log is
#   gzipped as captured, the n-gram tables cleaned (FN items follow).
# MOCK: SA14_SW=0 = a server without the int9b .. int14c switches (queue-ar/tools/mockrad; zsa14/mockrun-zsa14.sh); stage_short /
#   stage_pick are int8 switches, posted there too. DRYRUN=1 bash dsm-zsa14.sh : prints every command; checks the image literals, every
#   helper (+ selftests), the tables' and steps.py's md5s, the ngramshare files, the sidecars, the yamls, the disk; no server, no GPU.
